<title>SOUTH KOREA: SAMSUNG ELECT H1 NET AT 123.2 BLN WON.</title>
<headline>SAMSUNG ELECT H1 NET AT 123.2 BLN WON.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(In billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net			 123.2	 vs     453.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		8,908.8	 vs   8.713.7</p>
<p>    Profit before tax     153.7	 vs     531.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Samsung Electronics Co is an affiliate of the Samsung Group. A company statement said semiconductor sales fell to 2.56 trillion won during the first half period from 3.61 trillion won a year earlier. But six-month sales in info-tech areas rose to 2.05 trillion won from 1.05 trillion won a year ago. A company official said share capital increased to 117.56 billion shares at the end of June against 114.82 billion a year ago through rights issue offer and conversion of convertible bonds into common shares.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
